  "question": {
    "text": "The speed of sound in oxygen $\\left(\\mathrm{O}_2\\right)$ at a certain temperature is $460 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}$. The speed of sound in helium (He) at the same temperature will be (assumed both gases to be ideal)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "IYk5s",
      "text": "\n$460 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MEGKO",
      "text": "\n$500 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7ZRym",
      "text": "\n$650 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "0vn2I",
      "text": "\nNone of these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& v=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\gamma R T}{M}} \\\\\n& \\frac{V_1}{V_2}=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\gamma_1 M_2}{\\gamma_2 M_1}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{7}{5} \\times 4}{\\frac{5}{3} \\times 32}} \\\\\n& \\frac{460}{V_2}=\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{25 \\times 8}} \\Rightarrow \\quad v_2=\\frac{460 \\times 5 \\times 2 \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{21}}=1420\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
